The series LCR circuit is connected to voltage source V = 5 \sin(100 t), so peak voltage is V_0 = 5 V
Angular frequency of the AC source is \omega = 100 \text{ rad/s}
In a series LCR circuit, maximum current occurs under resonance condition: \omega L = \frac{1}{\omega C}
At resonance, the net inductive and capacitive reactances cancel: X_L - X_C = 0
Total impedance equals resistance: Z = R = 100 \ \Omega
Maximum current amplitude is I_0 = \frac{V_0}{R} = \frac{5}{100} = 0.05 \text{ A} = 50 \text{ mA}
From resonance condition, capacitance is C = \frac{1}{\omega^2 L}
Evaluating the circuit parameter gives 50
→ (50)

