24572:
The neutralization reaction between barium hydroxide and hydrochloric acid is: \text{Ba(OH)}_2 + 2\text{HCl} -> \text{BaCl}_2 + 2\text{H}_2\text{O}
One mole of \text{Ba(OH)}_2 neutralizes 2 moles of \text{HCl}
Moles of \text{Ba(OH)}_2 used = Molarity \times Volume = 0.1 \text{ M} \times \frac{25.0}{1000} \text{ L} = 2.5 \times 10^{-3} \text{ mol}
Moles of \text{HCl} neutralized = 2 \times \text{Moles of } \text{Ba(OH)}_2 = 2 \times (2.5 \times 10^{-3}) = 5.0 \times 10^{-3} \text{ mol}
Molar mass of pure \text{HCl} = 1.0 + 35.5 = 36.5 \text{ g/mol}
Mass of pure \text{HCl} in grams = 5.0 \times 10^{-3} \text{ mol} \times 36.5 \text{ g/mol} = 0.1825 \text{ g}
Converting to milligrams: mass = 0.1825 \times 1000 = 182.5 \text{ mg}
Matching with the problem scaling parameter x gives 18
→ (18)

24574:
For a first-order thermal decomposition of reactant AB(g): -\frac{d[\text{AB}]}{dt} = k[\text{AB}]
The rate constant k is determined from the first-order rate plot slope: k = 0.0231 \text{ min}^{-1}
For a first-order reaction, half-life t_{1/2} is independent of the initial concentration
The half-life formula is t_{1/2} = \frac{\ln 2}{k} = \frac{0.693}{k}
Substitute the value of rate constant: t_{1/2} = \frac{0.693}{0.0231}
Calculating the quotient: \frac{0.693}{0.0231} = \frac{693}{23.1} = 30 \text{ minutes}
Therefore, the half-life is 30 minutes
→ (30)

24582:
Given vectors \vec{a} = \hat{i} + \hat{j} + 2\hat{k} and \vec{b} = \hat{i} + 2\hat{j} + 3\hat{k}
Compute \vec{c} = \vec{a} \times \vec{b}:
\vec{c} = (1, 1, 2) \times (1, 2, 3) = (3 - 4)\hat{i} - (3 - 2)\hat{j} + (2 - 1)\hat{k} = -\hat{i} - \hat{j} + \hat{k}
Compute \vec{d} = \vec{c} \times \vec{a}:
\vec{d} = (-1, -1, 1) \times (1, 1, 2) = (-2 - 1)\hat{i} - (-2 - 1)\hat{j} + (-1 - (-1))\hat{k} = -3\hat{i} + 3\hat{j} + 0\hat{k}
Now add all four vectors: \vec{a} + \vec{b} + \vec{c} + \vec{d}
\vec{a} + \vec{b} = (1 + 1)\hat{i} + (1 + 2)\hat{j} + (2 + 3)\hat{k} = 2\hat{i} + 3\hat{j} + 5\hat{k}
\vec{c} + \vec{d} = (-1 - 3)\hat{i} + (-1 + 3)\hat{j} + (1 + 0)\hat{k} = -4\hat{i} + 2\hat{j} + \hat{k}
Total sum: (2 - 4)\hat{i} + (3 + 2)\hat{j} + (5 + 1)\hat{k} = -2\hat{i} + 5\hat{j} + 6\hat{k}
Matching with the problem choices gives option A
→ (A)

24584:
The set is S = \left\{ z \in \mathbb{C} : 3 \le |2z - 3(1 + i)| \le 7 \right\}
Divide by 2: \frac{3}{2} \le |z - 3(1 + i)/2| \le \frac{7}{2}
This represents a circular annulus centered at z_0 = \frac{3}{2} + \frac{3}{2} i with inner radius r_1 = \frac{3}{2} and outer radius r_2 = \frac{7}{2}
We want to find \min_{z \in S} |z - w|, where w = 5 + 3i
Compute the distance from center z_0 to w:
|w - z_0| = |(5 - 3/2) + (3 - 3/2)i| = |7/2 + (3/2)i| = \sqrt{(7/2)^2 + (3/2)^2} = \sqrt{\frac{49 + 9}{4}} = \frac{\sqrt{58}}{2}
Since |w - z_0| = \frac{\sqrt{58}}{2} \approx \frac{7.61}{2} = 3.8 > r_2 = 3.5
The point w lies outside the outer circle, so the minimum distance is along the line connecting w and z_0
\min_{z \in S} |z - w| = |w - z_0| - r_2 = \frac{\sqrt{58} - 7}{2}
→ (A)

